
usage: getGINAsat.py [-h] [-a {uaf5,gilmore,uafgina}]
                     [-s {terra,snpp,noaa21,noaa20,metop-c,metop-b,gcom-w,aws}] [-m MATCH]
                     [-l {level1,level2,scmi,mirs_awips,mirs_scmi,sst_awips,nucaps_level2,clavrx_scmi,mirs_level2,awips,NucapsAwips,edr_scmi,sst_geotif,raw,nucaps_level1,mod14,mirs_level2,mirs_geotif_l1,mirs_awips,level1_agg,level0-ipopp,geotiff_polar_l2,geotiff_polar_l1,geotiff_ngfs_l2,geotiff_level2,geotiff_l2,geotiff_l1,geotiff_gm_l2,geotiff_gm_l1,geotiff,FireAwips,fire,edr_geotiff_l1,clavrx_level2,clavrx_geotiff_l1,binary_slice,acspo_level2,,acspo_awips}]
                     [-t] [-ni] [-reg] [-f] [-bm BACKMINS] [-v]
                     {viirs,modis,metop,avhrr,atms,amsr2,all}
                     [{viirs,modis,metop,avhrr,atms,amsr2,all} ...]


######## Command Line Arguments ########

### Positional Arguments
One or more sensor types are required "positional" arguments that are not 
preceeded by an option indicator. Below are the only valid sensor choices:
- **sensor** (required, one or more): Satellite sensors to download.
  Choices: `viirs`, `modis`, `metop`, `avhrr`, `atms`, `amsr2`, `all`

### Optional Arguments
'-a`**, `--antenna`**: Antenna source. Choices: 'uaf5', 'gilmore', 'uafgina' (default: `all`)
`-s`**, `--satellite`**: Satellite source. Choices: 'terra', 'snpp', 'noaa21', 'noaa20', 
	'metop-c', 'metop-b', 'gcom-w', 'aws' (default: `all`)
-l`**, `--level`**: data processing level. Choices: 'level1`, 'level2', `scmi`, `mirs_awips`, 
	`mirs_scmi`, `sst_awips`, `nucaps_level2`, `clavrx_scmi`, `mirs_level2`, 
	`NucapsAwips`, `edr_scmi`, 'sst_geotif', 'raw', 'nucaps_level1', 'mod14', 
	'mirs_level2', 'mirs_geotif_l1', 'mirs_awips', 'level1_agg', 'level0-ipopp',
	'geotiff_polar_l2', 'geotiff_polar_l1', 'geotiff_ngfs_l2', 'geotiff_level2',
	'geotiff_l2', 'geotiff_l1', 'geotiff_gm_l2', 'geotiff_gm_l1', 'geotiff',
	'FireAwips', 'fire', 'edr_geotiff_l1', 'clavrx_level2', 'clavrx_geotiff_l1',
	'binary_slice', 'acspo_level2,', 'acspo_awips' (default: 'scmi')
`-m`**, `--match`**: Match substring in filename. (default: match everything)
'-t`, `--test`**: Use test NRT data stream. (flag)
`-ni`, `--noingest`: No AWIPS ingest, transfer file only. (flag)
`-reg`, `--regionalsat`: add 'Alaska_' prefix to regionalsat filename for for AWIPS
	to recognize and process. (flag)
`-f`, `--qcfilter`: Turn on image QC filter. (flag)
`-bm`**, `--backmins`**: Number of minutes back to consider. (default: `61`, type: int)
`-v`, `--verbose`: Verbose flag. (flag)
'-ver', '--version': Report the version number

Examples:

getGINAsat.py --level scmi viirs modis avhrr
       - retrieves any scmi formatted viirs, modis, or avhrr data from any satellite within 
	the default search time of the last 60 mins.

getGINAsat.py --satellite noaa20 -bm 85 viirs
       - retrieves any scmi (default) formatted viirs data from noaa20 within the specified 
	search time of the last 85 mins. 

getGINAsat.py --level mirs_scmi -bm 75 atms avhrr
       - retrieves any mirs products in awips format from atms or avhrr(AMSU-A/MHS)  within the 
	specified search time of the last 75 mins. 

getGINAsat.py --level scmi --test -bm 90 viirs modis
       - from the test NRT retrieves any SCMI tile formatted files viirs or modis from any 
	platform data within the specified search time of the last 90 mins.

getGINAsat.py -a uaf5 -l level2 -m CloudHeight -bm 45 -ni viirs
       - from only uaf5 antenna data retrieves viirs level2 data with filenames that match
	the "CloudHeight" string from only the uaf5 antenna that within the specified search
	time of the last 45 mins.

getGINAsat.py -a uaf5 -l edr_scmi -m AOD -t -bm 100 -ni all

#################   additional support script   #############################

getLatestSat_GINA.sh	- a wrapper script for running getGINAsat.py from cron that checks for 
                         multiple instances that might still be running and appends output to a 
                         log file.  Arguments are passed through to the python script, so 
			 all arguments listed above apply.

